event: values
data: {"messages":[{"content":"请把人员、车辆和停留行为映射成“闯入、聚集、滞留、逆行”等标准事件，并给出每个事件的匹配分。","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"human","name":null,"id":"c4f763de-5d7c-4121-95c2-06604b898a7b"},{"content":"<skill_system source=\"skill_router\">\nYou have access to skills that provide optimized workflows for specific tasks. Each skill contains best practices, frameworks, and references to additional resources.\n\n**Skill Availability Rules:**\n- Public skills listed in the base system prompt are available across turns.\n- Custom/domain skills are available only when listed in a current-turn routed <available_skills> section.\n- Ignore custom/domain skills mentioned in previous turns if they are not listed in the current turn.\n- Do not call tools associated with unavailable skills.\n- If a later current-turn routed_skill_prompt is injected by SkillRouter, its <available_skills> list recommends the custom/domain skills for this turn; public skills from the base prompt remain available as supporting workflows.\n- When SkillRouter ranking is disabled and scene filtering injects all skills for a scene, treat <available_skills> as an allowed candidate set. Select the specific skill or skills that match the current user request before loading skill files or executing workflows.\n\nScene skill filter result: SkillRouter ranking is disabled. Detected scene(s): video_surveillance. The listed custom/domain skills are all enabled skills for the detected scene. Treat them as an allowed candidate set, choose the specific matching skill or skills for the task, and then load only the chosen skill file(s). Public skills from the base prompt remain available.\nTask: 请把人员、车辆和停留行为映射成“闯入、聚集、滞留、逆行”等标准事件，并给出每个事件的匹配分。\n\n**Current Available Skills:**\n- The current <available_skills> list is empty.\n- No routed custom/domain skill matched this turn.\n- Public skills listed in the base system prompt remain available.\n\n**Override Scope:**\n- This routed <skill_system> lists recommended custom/domain skills for the current turn.\n- It does NOT replace the base system prompt.\n- Public skills listed in the base system prompt remain available for supporting operations.\n- When uploaded structured files (Excel, CSV, JSON, Parquet, or similar tabular evidence) are central to the user's request, use the public data-analysis skill first to inspect and extract facts before domain synthesis.\n- Continue following language_policy, clarification_system, working_directory, response_style, and critical_reminders from the base system prompt.\n\n**Progressive Loading Pattern:**\n1. When a user query matches an available skill's use case, first choose the concrete skill.\n2. Call `invoke_skill` in `prepare` mode for that selected skill to create and validate the SkillInputEnvelope and legacy invocation package.\n3. Read the returned skill file path and understand the skill's workflow and instructions.\n4. The skill file contains references to external resources under the same folder.\n5. Load referenced resources only when needed during execution.\n6. Follow the skill's instructions precisely.\n7. After legacy execution, call `invoke_skill` in `wrap_output` mode to normalize the result into SkillResult when a machine-readable Skill output is needed.\n\n**Mandatory Skill Execution Discipline:**\n- Calling `invoke_skill` in `prepare` mode is NOT sufficient. It only prepares the selected Skill invocation. After `prepare`, you MUST actually execute the selected Skill workflow.\n- After `invoke_skill(mode=\"prepare\")` returns `legacy_invocation.container_skill_file`, you MUST read that Skill file and treat it as the authoritative execution guide.\n- If the Skill provides scripts, commands, templates, references, or executable workflows, you MUST use those Skill-provided assets first.\n- Do NOT replace a matched Skill workflow with ad hoc Python, pandas, SQL, shell, or manual analysis code before attempting the Skill workflow.\n- For `data-analysis`, if `/mnt/skills/public/data-analysis/scripts/analyze.py` is available and the task is structured data analysis, you MUST call that script first for data inspection, SQL query, aggregation, statistics, or chart preparation. Do not write standalone pandas code for the same operation before trying this script.\n- Custom code is allowed only after one of these conditions is true:\n  1. the selected Skill file does not provide a suitable executable workflow;\n  2. the Skill-provided script or workflow has been attempted and failed;\n  3. the user explicitly requests custom code;\n  4. the required operation is clearly outside the Skill's documented capability.\n- When you fall back to custom code, briefly state that the Skill workflow was insufficient or failed, and continue from the Skill result or error.\n\n**Skill Loading Priority Rules:**\n- If a request clearly matches an available skill and also includes uploaded files, load the skill file before reading uploaded data files.\n- Do NOT read a full uploaded structured data file before loading the matched skill.\n- For uploaded structured data files, use small previews only when needed.\n- Prefer the matched skill's scripts, workflows, or tools for actual analysis.\n- Do not start by generating ad hoc JS, Python, SQL, or shell scripts when a matched skill exists.\n- Only improvise custom code after loading the matched skill and confirming the skill does not already provide a suitable workflow.\n\n**Skills are located at:** /mnt/skills\n\n<available_skills>\n</available_skills>\n\n</skill_system>","additional_kwargs":{"message_type":"routed_skill_prompt","internal":true},"response_metadata":{},"type":"human","name":"routing_skill_guidance","id":"0a3a9c6c-636b-4f6f-b49d-183c80882682"},{"content":"<system_reminder>\nUse the following current-turn intent and routing guidance when deciding whether to create or update todos. Treat it as planning context, not as a user request.\n<hidden_step source=\"intent_recognition\" title=\"意图识别\">\n改写后的任务：场景：视频监控。场景ID：video_surveillance\n识别场景：视频监控 (video_surveillance)；场景模式：single；候选场景：video_surveillance\n任务切分：\n- 请把人员、车辆和停留行为映射成“闯入、聚集、滞留、逆行”等标准事件，并给出每个事件的匹配分。\n任务规划：\n1. 解析视频监控原始帧序列或目标检测日志，提取人员与车辆的时空轨迹数据及基础运动特征（坐标、速度、航向角），输出结构化目标行为数据集。\n2. 结合安防巡检业务规范，定义“闯入、聚集、滞留、逆行”四类标准事件的判定依据与关键指标（如闯入划定禁入区域边界与穿越持续时间，聚集设定监测窗口内人员/车辆密度阈值，滞留明确最低驻留时长基准，逆行规定运动矢量与主干道流向的夹角偏差范围）。\n3. 基于已定义的事件判定口径，逐一对比目标轨迹特征与四类标准事件规则，采用空间重叠度、时间持续性与方向一致性算法计算匹配分，生成带有权重评分的初步映射结果集。\n4. 执行多事件交叉研判与分数归一化处理，筛选出各目标匹配分最高的唯一标准事件映射，剔除低置信度冗余记录，输出标准化事件匹配清单。\n5. 按照视频监控告警分析的交付规范，将最终映射关系与匹配分整合为结构化报表，供后续监控看板展示或异常处置流程调用。\n场景任务：\n- video_surveillance: 在视频监控场景下，我将把人员、车辆和停留行为映射为闯入、聚集、滞留、逆行等标准事件，并为每个事件输出匹配分。；参数：{'监控目标': '人员、车辆和停留行为', '输出形式': '匹配分'}\n已提取参数：{'监控目标': '人员、车辆和停留行为', '输出形式': '匹配分'}\n任务提示：\n- 提取必填参数：视频对象。需要分析的监控视频、摄像头、视频流、录像文件、实时画面、卡口视频或视频帧\n- 提取可选参数：监控目标。需要识别或分析的对象、行为或事件，如人员聚集、车辆违停、越界、烟火、异常停留、摔倒、入侵、打架、遗留物、通行计数等\n- 提取可选参数：时间范围。视频分析的起止时间、日期、时段、时刻或实时窗口\n- 提取可选参数：输出形式。用户期望的输出，如告警、截图、时间点清单、检测结果、表格、报告、标注说明或风险摘要\n</hidden_step>\n</system_reminder>","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"human","name":"todo_routing_guidance","id":"b697eb01-85ee-4505-99a8-61240cf06101"},{"content":"我来帮你把人员、车辆和停留行为映射到标准安防事件并计算匹配分。不过我首先需要确认一些信息：\n\n","additional_kwargs":{"refusal":null},"response_metadata":{"token_usage":{"completion_tokens":392,"prompt_tokens":10967,"total_tokens":11359,"completion_tokens_details":{"accepted_prediction_tokens":null,"audio_tokens":null,"reasoning_tokens":200,"rejected_prediction_tokens":null,"text_tokens":392},"prompt_tokens_details":{"audio_tokens":null,"cached_tokens":null,"text_tokens":10967}},"model_provider":"openai","model_name":"qwen3.6-35b-a3b","system_fingerprint":null,"id":"chatcmpl-1a383c2e-dd75-9008-8228-ff5b7d1368b5","finish_reason":"tool_calls","logprobs":null},"type":"ai","name":null,"id":"lc_run--019f8f62-9fde-7332-a9c8-e76864d2bc3b-0","tool_calls":[{"name":"ask_clarification","args":{"context":"要将目标行为映射为标准事件，我需要知道分析的视频源或数据源。","options":"[\"请上传监控视频文件\", \"我有检测/跟踪结果数据（CSV/JSON等）\", \"使用已有的本地数据集\", \"先给我一套通用的映射规则和评分模型\"]","question":"你需要分析的监控数据来源是什么？请提供以下任一内容：\n1. 监控视频文件路径\n2. 已有的人员/车辆检测结果（CSV/JSON格式）\n3. 轨迹跟踪日志\n4. 或者你希望我先给出一套通用的事件映射规则和评分模型？"},"id":"call_102f80619d6c43f9bbdf1cb6","type":"tool_call"}],"invalid_tool_calls":[],"usage_metadata":{"input_tokens":10967,"output_tokens":392,"total_tokens":11359,"input_token_details":{},"output_token_details":{"reasoning":200}}}],"thread_data":{"workspace_path":"/app/backend/.deer-flow/threads/088134d6-f21a-40a9-878e-051501adad4d/user-data/workspace","uploads_path":"/app/backend/.deer-flow/threads/088134d6-f21a-40a9-878e-051501adad4d/user-data/uploads","outputs_path":"/app/backend/.deer-flow/threads/088134d6-f21a-40a9-878e-051501adad4d/user-data/outputs"},"title":"事件映射评分","artifacts":[],"raw_messages":[{"content":"请把人员、车辆和停留行为映射成“闯入、聚集、滞留、逆行”等标准事件，并给出每个事件的匹配分。","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"human","name":null,"id":"c4f763de-5d7c-4121-95c2-06604b898a7b"},{"content":"<skill_system source=\"skill_router\">\nYou have access to skills that provide optimized workflows for specific tasks. Each skill contains best practices, frameworks, and references to additional resources.\n\n**Skill Availability Rules:**\n- Public skills listed in the base system prompt are available across turns.\n- Custom/domain skills are available only when listed in a current-turn routed <available_skills> section.\n- Ignore custom/domain skills mentioned in previous turns if they are not listed in the current turn.\n- Do not call tools associated with unavailable skills.\n- If a later current-turn routed_skill_prompt is injected by SkillRouter, its <available_skills> list recommends the custom/domain skills for this turn; public skills from the base prompt remain available as supporting workflows.\n- When SkillRouter ranking is disabled and scene filtering injects all skills for a scene, treat <available_skills> as an allowed candidate set. Select the specific skill or skills that match the current user request before loading skill files or executing workflows.\n\nScene skill filter result: SkillRouter ranking is disabled. Detected scene(s): video_surveillance. The listed custom/domain skills are all enabled skills for the detected scene. Treat them as an allowed candidate set, choose the specific matching skill or skills for the task, and then load only the chosen skill file(s). Public skills from the base prompt remain available.\nTask: 请把人员、车辆和停留行为映射成“闯入、聚集、滞留、逆行”等标准事件，并给出每个事件的匹配分。\n\n**Current Available Skills:**\n- The current <available_skills> list is empty.\n- No routed custom/domain skill matched this turn.\n- Public skills listed in the base system prompt remain available.\n\n**Override Scope:**\n- This routed <skill_system> lists recommended custom/domain skills for the current turn.\n- It does NOT replace the base system prompt.\n- Public skills listed in the base system prompt remain available for supporting operations.\n- When uploaded structured files (Excel, CSV, JSON, Parquet, or similar tabular evidence) are central to the user's request, use the public data-analysis skill first to inspect and extract facts before domain synthesis.\n- Continue following language_policy, clarification_system, working_directory, response_style, and critical_reminders from the base system prompt.\n\n**Progressive Loading Pattern:**\n1. When a user query matches an available skill's use case, first choose the concrete skill.\n2. Call `invoke_skill` in `prepare` mode for that selected skill to create and validate the SkillInputEnvelope and legacy invocation package.\n3. Read the returned skill file path and understand the skill's workflow and instructions.\n4. The skill file contains references to external resources under the same folder.\n5. Load referenced resources only when needed during execution.\n6. Follow the skill's instructions precisely.\n7. After legacy execution, call `invoke_skill` in `wrap_output` mode to normalize the result into SkillResult when a machine-readable Skill output is needed.\n\n**Mandatory Skill Execution Discipline:**\n- Calling `invoke_skill` in `prepare` mode is NOT sufficient. It only prepares the selected Skill invocation. After `prepare`, you MUST actually execute the selected Skill workflow.\n- After `invoke_skill(mode=\"prepare\")` returns `legacy_invocation.container_skill_file`, you MUST read that Skill file and treat it as the authoritative execution guide.\n- If the Skill provides scripts, commands, templates, references, or executable workflows, you MUST use those Skill-provided assets first.\n- Do NOT replace a matched Skill workflow with ad hoc Python, pandas, SQL, shell, or manual analysis code before attempting the Skill workflow.\n- For `data-analysis`, if `/mnt/skills/public/data-analysis/scripts/analyze.py` is available and the task is structured data analysis, you MUST call that script first for data inspection, SQL query, aggregation, statistics, or chart preparation. Do not write standalone pandas code for the same operation before trying this script.\n- Custom code is allowed only after one of these conditions is true:\n  1. the selected Skill file does not provide a suitable executable workflow;\n  2. the Skill-provided script or workflow has been attempted and failed;\n  3. the user explicitly requests custom code;\n  4. the required operation is clearly outside the Skill's documented capability.\n- When you fall back to custom code, briefly state that the Skill workflow was insufficient or failed, and continue from the Skill result or error.\n\n**Skill Loading Priority Rules:**\n- If a request clearly matches an available skill and also includes uploaded files, load the skill file before reading uploaded data files.\n- Do NOT read a full uploaded structured data file before loading the matched skill.\n- For uploaded structured data files, use small previews only when needed.\n- Prefer the matched skill's scripts, workflows, or tools for actual analysis.\n- Do not start by generating ad hoc JS, Python, SQL, or shell scripts when a matched skill exists.\n- Only improvise custom code after loading the matched skill and confirming the skill does not already provide a suitable workflow.\n\n**Skills are located at:** /mnt/skills\n\n<available_skills>\n</available_skills>\n\n</skill_system>","additional_kwargs":{"message_type":"routed_skill_prompt","internal":true},"response_metadata":{},"type":"human","name":"routing_skill_guidance","id":"0a3a9c6c-636b-4f6f-b49d-183c80882682"},{"content":"<system_reminder>\nUse the following current-turn intent and routing guidance when deciding whether to create or update todos. Treat it as planning context, not as a user request.\n<hidden_step source=\"intent_recognition\" title=\"意图识别\">\n改写后的任务：场景：视频监控。场景ID：video_surveillance\n识别场景：视频监控 (video_surveillance)；场景模式：single；候选场景：video_surveillance\n任务切分：\n- 请把人员、车辆和停留行为映射成“闯入、聚集、滞留、逆行”等标准事件，并给出每个事件的匹配分。\n任务规划：\n1. 解析视频监控原始帧序列或目标检测日志，提取人员与车辆的时空轨迹数据及基础运动特征（坐标、速度、航向角），输出结构化目标行为数据集。\n2. 结合安防巡检业务规范，定义“闯入、聚集、滞留、逆行”四类标准事件的判定依据与关键指标（如闯入划定禁入区域边界与穿越持续时间，聚集设定监测窗口内人员/车辆密度阈值，滞留明确最低驻留时长基准，逆行规定运动矢量与主干道流向的夹角偏差范围）。\n3. 基于已定义的事件判定口径，逐一对比目标轨迹特征与四类标准事件规则，采用空间重叠度、时间持续性与方向一致性算法计算匹配分，生成带有权重评分的初步映射结果集。\n4. 执行多事件交叉研判与分数归一化处理，筛选出各目标匹配分最高的唯一标准事件映射，剔除低置信度冗余记录，输出标准化事件匹配清单。\n5. 按照视频监控告警分析的交付规范，将最终映射关系与匹配分整合为结构化报表，供后续监控看板展示或异常处置流程调用。\n场景任务：\n- video_surveillance: 在视频监控场景下，我将把人员、车辆和停留行为映射为闯入、聚集、滞留、逆行等标准事件，并为每个事件输出匹配分。；参数：{'监控目标': '人员、车辆和停留行为', '输出形式': '匹配分'}\n已提取参数：{'监控目标': '人员、车辆和停留行为', '输出形式': '匹配分'}\n任务提示：\n- 提取必填参数：视频对象。需要分析的监控视频、摄像头、视频流、录像文件、实时画面、卡口视频或视频帧\n- 提取可选参数：监控目标。需要识别或分析的对象、行为或事件，如人员聚集、车辆违停、越界、烟火、异常停留、摔倒、入侵、打架、遗留物、通行计数等\n- 提取可选参数：时间范围。视频分析的起止时间、日期、时段、时刻或实时窗口\n- 提取可选参数：输出形式。用户期望的输出，如告警、截图、时间点清单、检测结果、表格、报告、标注说明或风险摘要\n</hidden_step>\n</system_reminder>","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"human","name":"todo_routing_guidance","id":"b697eb01-85ee-4505-99a8-61240cf06101"},{"content":"我来帮你把人员、车辆和停留行为映射到标准安防事件并计算匹配分。不过我首先需要确认一些信息：\n\n","additional_kwargs":{"refusal":null},"response_metadata":{"token_usage":{"completion_tokens":392,"prompt_tokens":10967,"total_tokens":11359,"completion_tokens_details":{"accepted_prediction_tokens":null,"audio_tokens":null,"reasoning_tokens":200,"rejected_prediction_tokens":null,"text_tokens":392},"prompt_tokens_details":{"audio_tokens":null,"cached_tokens":null,"text_tokens":10967}},"model_provider":"openai","model_name":"qwen3.6-35b-a3b","system_fingerprint":null,"id":"chatcmpl-1a383c2e-dd75-9008-8228-ff5b7d1368b5","finish_reason":"tool_calls","logprobs":null},"type":"ai","name":null,"id":"lc_run--019f8f62-9fde-7332-a9c8-e76864d2bc3b-0","tool_calls":[{"name":"ask_clarification","args":{"context":"要将目标行为映射为标准事件，我需要知道分析的视频源或数据源。","options":"[\"请上传监控视频文件\", \"我有检测/跟踪结果数据（CSV/JSON等）\", \"使用已有的本地数据集\", \"先给我一套通用的映射规则和评分模型\"]","question":"你需要分析的监控数据来源是什么？请提供以下任一内容：\n1. 监控视频文件路径\n2. 已有的人员/车辆检测结果（CSV/JSON格式）\n3. 轨迹跟踪日志\n4. 或者你希望我先给出一套通用的事件映射规则和评分模型？"},"id":"call_102f80619d6c43f9bbdf1cb6","type":"tool_call"}],"invalid_tool_calls":[],"usage_metadata":{"input_tokens":10967,"output_tokens":392,"total_tokens":11359,"input_token_details":{},"output_token_details":{"reasoning":200}}}],"viewed_images":{},"intent_context":{"intent":"task","original_query":"请把人员、车辆和停留行为映射成“闯入、聚集、滞留、逆行”等标准事件，并给出每个事件的匹配分。","normalized_query":"请把人员、车辆和停留行为映射成“闯入、聚集、滞留、逆行”等标准事件，并给出每个事件的匹配分。","routing_query":"场景：视频监控。场景ID：video_surveillance。场景说明：视频监控、摄像头、监控录像、视频流、实时画面、视频帧、卡口、安防巡检、目标检测、行为识别、事件发现和监控告警分析场景。需要识别参数：视频对象、监控目标、时间范围、输出形式。用户原始问题：在视频监控场景下，我将把人员、车辆和停留行为映射为闯入、聚集、滞留、逆行等标准事件，并为每个事件输出匹配分","scene":"video_surveillance","scene_name":"视频监控","params":{"监控目标":"人员、车辆和停留行为","输出形式":"匹配分"},"scene_mode":"single","scenes":["video_surveillance"],"task_spans":[{"task_span_id":"span_ff4f13","text":"请把人员、车辆和停留行为映射成“闯入、聚集、滞留、逆行”等标准事件，并给出每个事件的匹配分。"}],"planning_steps":[{"task_span_id":"span_f6a080","text":"解析视频监控原始帧序列或目标检测日志，提取人员与车辆的时空轨迹数据及基础运动特征（坐标、速度、航向角），输出结构化目标行为数据集。"},{"task_span_id":"span_c7b9c9","text":"结合安防巡检业务规范，定义“闯入、聚集、滞留、逆行”四类标准事件的判定依据与关键指标（如闯入划定禁入区域边界与穿越持续时间，聚集设定监测窗口内人员/车辆密度阈值，滞留明确最低驻留时长基准，逆行规定运动矢量与主干道流向的夹角偏差范围）。"},{"task_span_id":"span_ac1f32","text":"基于已定义的事件判定口径，逐一对比目标轨迹特征与四类标准事件规则，采用空间重叠度、时间持续性与方向一致性算法计算匹配分，生成带有权重评分的初步映射结果集。"},{"task_span_id":"span_60d29e","text":"执行多事件交叉研判与分数归一化处理，筛选出各目标匹配分最高的唯一标准事件映射，剔除低置信度冗余记录，输出标准化事件匹配清单。"},{"task_span_id":"span_2a055c","text":"按照视频监控告警分析的交付规范，将最终映射关系与匹配分整合为结构化报表，供后续监控看板展示或异常处置流程调用。"}],"scene_tasks":[{"sub_task_id":"sub_f1aa44","scene":"video_surveillance","scene_name":"视频监控","text":"在视频监控场景下，我将把人员、车辆和停留行为映射为闯入、聚集、滞留、逆行等标准事件，并为每个事件输出匹配分。","params":{"监控目标":"人员、车辆和停留行为","输出形式":"匹配分"}}],"sub_tasks":[{"sub_task_id":"sub_f1aa44","scene":"video_surveillance","scene_name":"视频监控","text":"在视频监控场景下，我将把人员、车辆和停留行为映射为闯入、聚集、滞留、逆行等标准事件，并为每个事件输出匹配分。","params":{"监控目标":"人员、车辆和停留行为","输出形式":"匹配分"}}],"task_hints":["提取必填参数：视频对象。需要分析的监控视频、摄像头、视频流、录像文件、实时画面、卡口视频或视频帧","提取可选参数：监控目标。需要识别或分析的对象、行为或事件，如人员聚集、车辆违停、越界、烟火、异常停留、摔倒、入侵、打架、遗留物、通行计数等","提取可选参数：时间范围。视频分析的起止时间、日期、时段、时刻或实时窗口","提取可选参数：输出形式。用户期望的输出，如告警、截图、时间点清单、检测结果、表格、报告、标注说明或风险摘要"],"mentioned_skill_ids":[],"confidence":0.9,"reason":"llm_scene_slot_rewrite","_source_message_key":"id:c4f763de-5d7c-4121-95c2-06604b898a7b"},"routing_context":{"route_mode":"scene_filter","trigger":false,"primary_goal":"请把人员、车辆和停留行为映射成“闯入、聚集、滞留、逆行”等标准事件，并给出每个事件的匹配分。","scene_tasks":[{"scene_task_id":"task_001","segment_id":"seg_001","segment_text":"请把人员、车辆和停留行为映射成“闯入、聚集、滞留、逆行”等标准事件，并给出每个事件的匹配分。","scene":"video_surveillance","input_refs":[],"task_types":[],"selected_skills":[],"expected_outputs":[],"depends_on":[]}],"global_selected_skills":[],"default_public_skill_ids":[],"global_allowed_tools":[],"confidence":0.0,"route_reason":"SkillRouter disabled; injected all custom skills for detected intent scene as LeadAgent candidate skills","allowed_skills":[],"selection_owner":"lead_agent","_source_message_key":"id:c4f763de-5d7c-4121-95c2-06604b898a7b"},"dialogue_context":{"act":"new_task","confidence":0.7,"reason":"no_pending_action_match","parsed_answer":null,"pending_action_id":null,"resume_intent_context":null,"resume_routing_context":null,"metadata":{}},"final_scope_skill_ids":[],"allowed_tool_names":[]}

event: values
data: {"messages":[{"content":"请把人员、车辆和停留行为映射成“闯入、聚集、滞留、逆行”等标准事件，并给出每个事件的匹配分。","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"human","name":null,"id":"c4f763de-5d7c-4121-95c2-06604b898a7b"},{"content":"<skill_system source=\"skill_router\">\nYou have access to skills that provide optimized workflows for specific tasks. Each skill contains best practices, frameworks, and references to additional resources.\n\n**Skill Availability Rules:**\n- Public skills listed in the base system prompt are available across turns.\n- Custom/domain skills are available only when listed in a current-turn routed <available_skills> section.\n- Ignore custom/domain skills mentioned in previous turns if they are not listed in the current turn.\n- Do not call tools associated with unavailable skills.\n- If a later current-turn routed_skill_prompt is injected by SkillRouter, its <available_skills> list recommends the custom/domain skills for this turn; public skills from the base prompt remain available as supporting workflows.\n- When SkillRouter ranking is disabled and scene filtering injects all skills for a scene, treat <available_skills> as an allowed candidate set. Select the specific skill or skills that match the current user request before loading skill files or executing workflows.\n\nScene skill filter result: SkillRouter ranking is disabled. Detected scene(s): video_surveillance. The listed custom/domain skills are all enabled skills for the detected scene. Treat them as an allowed candidate set, choose the specific matching skill or skills for the task, and then load only the chosen skill file(s). Public skills from the base prompt remain available.\nTask: 请把人员、车辆和停留行为映射成“闯入、聚集、滞留、逆行”等标准事件，并给出每个事件的匹配分。\n\n**Current Available Skills:**\n- The current <available_skills> list is empty.\n- No routed custom/domain skill matched this turn.\n- Public skills listed in the base system prompt remain available.\n\n**Override Scope:**\n- This routed <skill_system> lists recommended custom/domain skills for the current turn.\n- It does NOT replace the base system prompt.\n- Public skills listed in the base system prompt remain available for supporting operations.\n- When uploaded structured files (Excel, CSV, JSON, Parquet, or similar tabular evidence) are central to the user's request, use the public data-analysis skill first to inspect and extract facts before domain synthesis.\n- Continue following language_policy, clarification_system, working_directory, response_style, and critical_reminders from the base system prompt.\n\n**Progressive Loading Pattern:**\n1. When a user query matches an available skill's use case, first choose the concrete skill.\n2. Call `invoke_skill` in `prepare` mode for that selected skill to create and validate the SkillInputEnvelope and legacy invocation package.\n3. Read the returned skill file path and understand the skill's workflow and instructions.\n4. The skill file contains references to external resources under the same folder.\n5. Load referenced resources only when needed during execution.\n6. Follow the skill's instructions precisely.\n7. After legacy execution, call `invoke_skill` in `wrap_output` mode to normalize the result into SkillResult when a machine-readable Skill output is needed.\n\n**Mandatory Skill Execution Discipline:**\n- Calling `invoke_skill` in `prepare` mode is NOT sufficient. It only prepares the selected Skill invocation. After `prepare`, you MUST actually execute the selected Skill workflow.\n- After `invoke_skill(mode=\"prepare\")` returns `legacy_invocation.container_skill_file`, you MUST read that Skill file and treat it as the authoritative execution guide.\n- If the Skill provides scripts, commands, templates, references, or executable workflows, you MUST use those Skill-provided assets first.\n- Do NOT replace a matched Skill workflow with ad hoc Python, pandas, SQL, shell, or manual analysis code before attempting the Skill workflow.\n- For `data-analysis`, if `/mnt/skills/public/data-analysis/scripts/analyze.py` is available and the task is structured data analysis, you MUST call that script first for data inspection, SQL query, aggregation, statistics, or chart preparation. Do not write standalone pandas code for the same operation before trying this script.\n- Custom code is allowed only after one of these conditions is true:\n  1. the selected Skill file does not provide a suitable executable workflow;\n  2. the Skill-provided script or workflow has been attempted and failed;\n  3. the user explicitly requests custom code;\n  4. the required operation is clearly outside the Skill's documented capability.\n- When you fall back to custom code, briefly state that the Skill workflow was insufficient or failed, and continue from the Skill result or error.\n\n**Skill Loading Priority Rules:**\n- If a request clearly matches an available skill and also includes uploaded files, load the skill file before reading uploaded data files.\n- Do NOT read a full uploaded structured data file before loading the matched skill.\n- For uploaded structured data files, use small previews only when needed.\n- Prefer the matched skill's scripts, workflows, or tools for actual analysis.\n- Do not start by generating ad hoc JS, Python, SQL, or shell scripts when a matched skill exists.\n- Only improvise custom code after loading the matched skill and confirming the skill does not already provide a suitable workflow.\n\n**Skills are located at:** /mnt/skills\n\n<available_skills>\n</available_skills>\n\n</skill_system>","additional_kwargs":{"message_type":"routed_skill_prompt","internal":true},"response_metadata":{},"type":"human","name":"routing_skill_guidance","id":"0a3a9c6c-636b-4f6f-b49d-183c80882682"},{"content":"<system_reminder>\nUse the following current-turn intent and routing guidance when deciding whether to create or update todos. Treat it as planning context, not as a user request.\n<hidden_step source=\"intent_recognition\" title=\"意图识别\">\n改写后的任务：场景：视频监控。场景ID：video_surveillance\n识别场景：视频监控 (video_surveillance)；场景模式：single；候选场景：video_surveillance\n任务切分：\n- 请把人员、车辆和停留行为映射成“闯入、聚集、滞留、逆行”等标准事件，并给出每个事件的匹配分。\n任务规划：\n1. 解析视频监控原始帧序列或目标检测日志，提取人员与车辆的时空轨迹数据及基础运动特征（坐标、速度、航向角），输出结构化目标行为数据集。\n2. 结合安防巡检业务规范，定义“闯入、聚集、滞留、逆行”四类标准事件的判定依据与关键指标（如闯入划定禁入区域边界与穿越持续时间，聚集设定监测窗口内人员/车辆密度阈值，滞留明确最低驻留时长基准，逆行规定运动矢量与主干道流向的夹角偏差范围）。\n3. 基于已定义的事件判定口径，逐一对比目标轨迹特征与四类标准事件规则，采用空间重叠度、时间持续性与方向一致性算法计算匹配分，生成带有权重评分的初步映射结果集。\n4. 执行多事件交叉研判与分数归一化处理，筛选出各目标匹配分最高的唯一标准事件映射，剔除低置信度冗余记录，输出标准化事件匹配清单。\n5. 按照视频监控告警分析的交付规范，将最终映射关系与匹配分整合为结构化报表，供后续监控看板展示或异常处置流程调用。\n场景任务：\n- video_surveillance: 在视频监控场景下，我将把人员、车辆和停留行为映射为闯入、聚集、滞留、逆行等标准事件，并为每个事件输出匹配分。；参数：{'监控目标': '人员、车辆和停留行为', '输出形式': '匹配分'}\n已提取参数：{'监控目标': '人员、车辆和停留行为', '输出形式': '匹配分'}\n任务提示：\n- 提取必填参数：视频对象。需要分析的监控视频、摄像头、视频流、录像文件、实时画面、卡口视频或视频帧\n- 提取可选参数：监控目标。需要识别或分析的对象、行为或事件，如人员聚集、车辆违停、越界、烟火、异常停留、摔倒、入侵、打架、遗留物、通行计数等\n- 提取可选参数：时间范围。视频分析的起止时间、日期、时段、时刻或实时窗口\n- 提取可选参数：输出形式。用户期望的输出，如告警、截图、时间点清单、检测结果、表格、报告、标注说明或风险摘要\n</hidden_step>\n</system_reminder>","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"human","name":"todo_routing_guidance","id":"b697eb01-85ee-4505-99a8-61240cf06101"},{"content":"我来帮你把人员、车辆和停留行为映射到标准安防事件并计算匹配分。不过我首先需要确认一些信息：\n\n","additional_kwargs":{"refusal":null},"response_metadata":{"token_usage":{"completion_tokens":392,"prompt_tokens":10967,"total_tokens":11359,"completion_tokens_details":{"accepted_prediction_tokens":null,"audio_tokens":null,"reasoning_tokens":200,"rejected_prediction_tokens":null,"text_tokens":392},"prompt_tokens_details":{"audio_tokens":null,"cached_tokens":null,"text_tokens":10967}},"model_provider":"openai","model_name":"qwen3.6-35b-a3b","system_fingerprint":null,"id":"chatcmpl-1a383c2e-dd75-9008-8228-ff5b7d1368b5","finish_reason":"tool_calls","logprobs":null},"type":"ai","name":null,"id":"lc_run--019f8f62-9fde-7332-a9c8-e76864d2bc3b-0","tool_calls":[{"name":"ask_clarification","args":{"context":"要将目标行为映射为标准事件，我需要知道分析的视频源或数据源。","options":"[\"请上传监控视频文件\", \"我有检测/跟踪结果数据（CSV/JSON等）\", \"使用已有的本地数据集\", \"先给我一套通用的映射规则和评分模型\"]","question":"你需要分析的监控数据来源是什么？请提供以下任一内容：\n1. 监控视频文件路径\n2. 已有的人员/车辆检测结果（CSV/JSON格式）\n3. 轨迹跟踪日志\n4. 或者你希望我先给出一套通用的事件映射规则和评分模型？"},"id":"call_102f80619d6c43f9bbdf1cb6","type":"tool_call"}],"invalid_tool_calls":[],"usage_metadata":{"input_tokens":10967,"output_tokens":392,"total_tokens":11359,"input_token_details":{},"output_token_details":{"reasoning":200}}},{"content":"❓ 要将目标行为映射为标准事件，我需要知道分析的视频源或数据源。\n\n你需要分析的监控数据来源是什么？请提供以下任一内容：\n1. 监控视频文件路径\n2. 已有的人员/车辆检测结果（CSV/JSON格式）\n3. 轨迹跟踪日志\n4. 或者你希望我先给出一套通用的事件映射规则和评分模型？\n\n  1. 请上传监控视频文件\n  2. 我有检测/跟踪结果数据（CSV/JSON等）\n  3. 使用已有的本地数据集\n  4. 先给我一套通用的映射规则和评分模型","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"tool","name":"ask_clarification","id":"6b4deae8-5ecb-49db-989f-811609eec84b","tool_call_id":"call_102f80619d6c43f9bbdf1cb6","artifact":null,"status":"success"}],"thread_data":{"workspace_path":"/app/backend/.deer-flow/threads/088134d6-f21a-40a9-878e-051501adad4d/user-data/workspace","uploads_path":"/app/backend/.deer-flow/threads/088134d6-f21a-40a9-878e-051501adad4d/user-data/uploads","outputs_path":"/app/backend/.deer-flow/threads/088134d6-f21a-40a9-878e-051501adad4d/user-data/outputs"},"title":"事件映射评分","artifacts":[],"raw_messages":[{"content":"请把人员、车辆和停留行为映射成“闯入、聚集、滞留、逆行”等标准事件，并给出每个事件的匹配分。","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"human","name":null,"id":"c4f763de-5d7c-4121-95c2-06604b898a7b"},{"content":"<skill_system source=\"skill_router\">\nYou have access to skills that provide optimized workflows for specific tasks. Each skill contains best practices, frameworks, and references to additional resources.\n\n**Skill Availability Rules:**\n- Public skills listed in the base system prompt are available across turns.\n- Custom/domain skills are available only when listed in a current-turn routed <available_skills> section.\n- Ignore custom/domain skills mentioned in previous turns if they are not listed in the current turn.\n- Do not call tools associated with unavailable skills.\n- If a later current-turn routed_skill_prompt is injected by SkillRouter, its <available_skills> list recommends the custom/domain skills for this turn; public skills from the base prompt remain available as supporting workflows.\n- When SkillRouter ranking is disabled and scene filtering injects all skills for a scene, treat <available_skills> as an allowed candidate set. Select the specific skill or skills that match the current user request before loading skill files or executing workflows.\n\nScene skill filter result: SkillRouter ranking is disabled. Detected scene(s): video_surveillance. The listed custom/domain skills are all enabled skills for the detected scene. Treat them as an allowed candidate set, choose the specific matching skill or skills for the task, and then load only the chosen skill file(s). Public skills from the base prompt remain available.\nTask: 请把人员、车辆和停留行为映射成“闯入、聚集、滞留、逆行”等标准事件，并给出每个事件的匹配分。\n\n**Current Available Skills:**\n- The current <available_skills> list is empty.\n- No routed custom/domain skill matched this turn.\n- Public skills listed in the base system prompt remain available.\n\n**Override Scope:**\n- This routed <skill_system> lists recommended custom/domain skills for the current turn.\n- It does NOT replace the base system prompt.\n- Public skills listed in the base system prompt remain available for supporting operations.\n- When uploaded structured files (Excel, CSV, JSON, Parquet, or similar tabular evidence) are central to the user's request, use the public data-analysis skill first to inspect and extract facts before domain synthesis.\n- Continue following language_policy, clarification_system, working_directory, response_style, and critical_reminders from the base system prompt.\n\n**Progressive Loading Pattern:**\n1. When a user query matches an available skill's use case, first choose the concrete skill.\n2. Call `invoke_skill` in `prepare` mode for that selected skill to create and validate the SkillInputEnvelope and legacy invocation package.\n3. Read the returned skill file path and understand the skill's workflow and instructions.\n4. The skill file contains references to external resources under the same folder.\n5. Load referenced resources only when needed during execution.\n6. Follow the skill's instructions precisely.\n7. After legacy execution, call `invoke_skill` in `wrap_output` mode to normalize the result into SkillResult when a machine-readable Skill output is needed.\n\n**Mandatory Skill Execution Discipline:**\n- Calling `invoke_skill` in `prepare` mode is NOT sufficient. It only prepares the selected Skill invocation. After `prepare`, you MUST actually execute the selected Skill workflow.\n- After `invoke_skill(mode=\"prepare\")` returns `legacy_invocation.container_skill_file`, you MUST read that Skill file and treat it as the authoritative execution guide.\n- If the Skill provides scripts, commands, templates, references, or executable workflows, you MUST use those Skill-provided assets first.\n- Do NOT replace a matched Skill workflow with ad hoc Python, pandas, SQL, shell, or manual analysis code before attempting the Skill workflow.\n- For `data-analysis`, if `/mnt/skills/public/data-analysis/scripts/analyze.py` is available and the task is structured data analysis, you MUST call that script first for data inspection, SQL query, aggregation, statistics, or chart preparation. Do not write standalone pandas code for the same operation before trying this script.\n- Custom code is allowed only after one of these conditions is true:\n  1. the selected Skill file does not provide a suitable executable workflow;\n  2. the Skill-provided script or workflow has been attempted and failed;\n  3. the user explicitly requests custom code;\n  4. the required operation is clearly outside the Skill's documented capability.\n- When you fall back to custom code, briefly state that the Skill workflow was insufficient or failed, and continue from the Skill result or error.\n\n**Skill Loading Priority Rules:**\n- If a request clearly matches an available skill and also includes uploaded files, load the skill file before reading uploaded data files.\n- Do NOT read a full uploaded structured data file before loading the matched skill.\n- For uploaded structured data files, use small previews only when needed.\n- Prefer the matched skill's scripts, workflows, or tools for actual analysis.\n- Do not start by generating ad hoc JS, Python, SQL, or shell scripts when a matched skill exists.\n- Only improvise custom code after loading the matched skill and confirming the skill does not already provide a suitable workflow.\n\n**Skills are located at:** /mnt/skills\n\n<available_skills>\n</available_skills>\n\n</skill_system>","additional_kwargs":{"message_type":"routed_skill_prompt","internal":true},"response_metadata":{},"type":"human","name":"routing_skill_guidance","id":"0a3a9c6c-636b-4f6f-b49d-183c80882682"},{"content":"<system_reminder>\nUse the following current-turn intent and routing guidance when deciding whether to create or update todos. Treat it as planning context, not as a user request.\n<hidden_step source=\"intent_recognition\" title=\"意图识别\">\n改写后的任务：场景：视频监控。场景ID：video_surveillance\n识别场景：视频监控 (video_surveillance)；场景模式：single；候选场景：video_surveillance\n任务切分：\n- 请把人员、车辆和停留行为映射成“闯入、聚集、滞留、逆行”等标准事件，并给出每个事件的匹配分。\n任务规划：\n1. 解析视频监控原始帧序列或目标检测日志，提取人员与车辆的时空轨迹数据及基础运动特征（坐标、速度、航向角），输出结构化目标行为数据集。\n2. 结合安防巡检业务规范，定义“闯入、聚集、滞留、逆行”四类标准事件的判定依据与关键指标（如闯入划定禁入区域边界与穿越持续时间，聚集设定监测窗口内人员/车辆密度阈值，滞留明确最低驻留时长基准，逆行规定运动矢量与主干道流向的夹角偏差范围）。\n3. 基于已定义的事件判定口径，逐一对比目标轨迹特征与四类标准事件规则，采用空间重叠度、时间持续性与方向一致性算法计算匹配分，生成带有权重评分的初步映射结果集。\n4. 执行多事件交叉研判与分数归一化处理，筛选出各目标匹配分最高的唯一标准事件映射，剔除低置信度冗余记录，输出标准化事件匹配清单。\n5. 按照视频监控告警分析的交付规范，将最终映射关系与匹配分整合为结构化报表，供后续监控看板展示或异常处置流程调用。\n场景任务：\n- video_surveillance: 在视频监控场景下，我将把人员、车辆和停留行为映射为闯入、聚集、滞留、逆行等标准事件，并为每个事件输出匹配分。；参数：{'监控目标': '人员、车辆和停留行为', '输出形式': '匹配分'}\n已提取参数：{'监控目标': '人员、车辆和停留行为', '输出形式': '匹配分'}\n任务提示：\n- 提取必填参数：视频对象。需要分析的监控视频、摄像头、视频流、录像文件、实时画面、卡口视频或视频帧\n- 提取可选参数：监控目标。需要识别或分析的对象、行为或事件，如人员聚集、车辆违停、越界、烟火、异常停留、摔倒、入侵、打架、遗留物、通行计数等\n- 提取可选参数：时间范围。视频分析的起止时间、日期、时段、时刻或实时窗口\n- 提取可选参数：输出形式。用户期望的输出，如告警、截图、时间点清单、检测结果、表格、报告、标注说明或风险摘要\n</hidden_step>\n</system_reminder>","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"human","name":"todo_routing_guidance","id":"b697eb01-85ee-4505-99a8-61240cf06101"},{"content":"我来帮你把人员、车辆和停留行为映射到标准安防事件并计算匹配分。不过我首先需要确认一些信息：\n\n","additional_kwargs":{"refusal":null},"response_metadata":{"token_usage":{"completion_tokens":392,"prompt_tokens":10967,"total_tokens":11359,"completion_tokens_details":{"accepted_prediction_tokens":null,"audio_tokens":null,"reasoning_tokens":200,"rejected_prediction_tokens":null,"text_tokens":392},"prompt_tokens_details":{"audio_tokens":null,"cached_tokens":null,"text_tokens":10967}},"model_provider":"openai","model_name":"qwen3.6-35b-a3b","system_fingerprint":null,"id":"chatcmpl-1a383c2e-dd75-9008-8228-ff5b7d1368b5","finish_reason":"tool_calls","logprobs":null},"type":"ai","name":null,"id":"lc_run--019f8f62-9fde-7332-a9c8-e76864d2bc3b-0","tool_calls":[{"name":"ask_clarification","args":{"context":"要将目标行为映射为标准事件，我需要知道分析的视频源或数据源。","options":"[\"请上传监控视频文件\", \"我有检测/跟踪结果数据（CSV/JSON等）\", \"使用已有的本地数据集\", \"先给我一套通用的映射规则和评分模型\"]","question":"你需要分析的监控数据来源是什么？请提供以下任一内容：\n1. 监控视频文件路径\n2. 已有的人员/车辆检测结果（CSV/JSON格式）\n3. 轨迹跟踪日志\n4. 或者你希望我先给出一套通用的事件映射规则和评分模型？"},"id":"call_102f80619d6c43f9bbdf1cb6","type":"tool_call"}],"invalid_tool_calls":[],"usage_metadata":{"input_tokens":10967,"output_tokens":392,"total_tokens":11359,"input_token_details":{},"output_token_details":{"reasoning":200}}},{"content":"❓ 要将目标行为映射为标准事件，我需要知道分析的视频源或数据源。\n\n你需要分析的监控数据来源是什么？请提供以下任一内容：\n1. 监控视频文件路径\n2. 已有的人员/车辆检测结果（CSV/JSON格式）\n3. 轨迹跟踪日志\n4. 或者你希望我先给出一套通用的事件映射规则和评分模型？\n\n  1. 请上传监控视频文件\n  2. 我有检测/跟踪结果数据（CSV/JSON等）\n  3. 使用已有的本地数据集\n  4. 先给我一套通用的映射规则和评分模型","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"tool","name":"ask_clarification","id":"6b4deae8-5ecb-49db-989f-811609eec84b","tool_c